# | msgid "cmd.profile.description"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:790
msgid "cmd.config.reload.description"
msgstr "Re-read `config.toml` from disk without restarting."

# | msgid "cmd.profile.help"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:791
msgid "cmd.config.reload.help"
msgstr ""
"Re-read `config.toml` from disk and apply any changes without restarting "
"the bot.\n"
"\n"
"Use this after editing `config.toml` by hand while the bot is running. "
"The file is re-parsed, validated, and all settings are updated in memory."
"\n"
"\n"
"Safe settings (such as `bot.prefix` or logging levels) update "
"immediately. Settings that require a restart to fully take effect still "
"need one.\n"
"\n"
"If the file is invalid (malformed syntax or bad values), the reload is "
"rejected and the bot keeps using the previous valid config. Check the bot"
" logs for details about what went wrong.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples**\n"
"- `/config reload` — re-read `config.toml` after editing it by hand\n"
"- Use after changing the bot token or database URI so the new values take"
" effect"

# | msgid "cmd.profile.name"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:789
msgid "cmd.config.reload.name"
msgstr "reload"

# | msgid "cmd.close.description"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:647
msgid "cmd.config.set.description"
msgstr "Change a config value with smart parsing for any type."

# | msgid "cmd.close.help"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:648
msgid "cmd.config.set.help"
msgstr ""
"Change a config value. The value is parsed intelligently based on what "
"you type:\n"
"\n"
"**Simple values**\n"
"- Booleans: `true` or `false`\n"
"- Numbers: `42`, `3.14`, `0`\n"
"- Strings: `hello`, `\"quoted string with spaces\"`\n"
"- Arrays: `[1, 2, 3]`\n"
"- Inline tables: `{key = \"value\"}`\n"
"\n"
"**Batch operations for collections (lists, sets, dicts)**\n"
"- `+value` — add an item to a list or set\n"
"- `-value` — remove an item from a list or set\n"
"- `+key=value` — add or update a key-value pair in a dict\n"
"- `-key` — remove a key from a dict\n"
"- Combine multiple: `+a -b +c=d`\n"
"\n"
"Each operation is validated before writing to `config.toml`. Changes take"
" effect after a restart.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples**\n"
"- `/config set bot.prefix \"!\"` — change the bot prefix\n"
"- `/config set bot.respond_bot_mention false` — disable mention responses"
"\n"
"- `/config set permission.overrides +reply=staff` — allow staff to reply\n"
"- `/config set permission.overrides +reply=staff -close` — set reply to "
"staff and remove close override"

# | msgid "cmd.close.name"
#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:646
msgid "cmd.config.set.name"
msgstr "set"

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:596
msgid "cmd.config.show.description"
msgstr "Browse all config keys and their current values."

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:597
msgid "cmd.config.show.help"
msgstr ""
"Browse all config keys and their current values in an interactive menu.\n"
"\n"
"With no key specified, opens a paginated browser listing every available "
"setting. Use the dropdown or prev/next buttons to navigate. Click a key "
"to see its type, description, and current value.\n"
"\n"
"With a key specified, the browser opens focused on that key's detail "
"view.\n"
"\n"
"Secret values (like the bot token) are displayed as `**********`. "
"Settings that can only be changed by editing `config.toml` directly are "
"marked with `*`.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples**\n"
"- `/config show` — browse all settings\n"
"- `/config show bot.prefix` — jump to the prefix key\n"
"- `/config show permission.overrides` — jump to permission overrides"

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:595
msgid "cmd.config.show.name"
msgstr "show"

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:726
msgid "cmd.config.unset.description"
msgstr "Reset a config key to its built-in default value."

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:727
msgid "cmd.config.unset.help"
msgstr ""
"Reset a config key to its built-in default value.\n"
"\n"
"Removes the key from `config.toml` and re-validates. The field's default "
"value fills in automatically. Useful when you have changed a setting and "
"want to go back to the default without knowing what the default is.\n"
"\n"
"Fields without defaults cannot be unset. Read-only keys (like `version`) "
"are also rejected.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples**\n"
"- `/config unset bot.prefix` — reset prefix to default `?`\n"
"- `/config unset bot.respond_bot_mention` — reset to default `true`"

#: modmail/cogs/utility/commands/config.py:725
msgid "cmd.config.unset.name"
msgstr "unset"

